WEBVTT

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:12.330
A countless number of amulets,
a suspicious vase,

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.910
and...

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.450
--Gross! Oh god, it reeks!
--A black liquid that reeks of rotten meat,

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:21.580
a haggardly man's wailing,
and Mizuho in a shrine maiden's outfit!

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.870
--Ritsukooo!
--How am I supposed to describe
all this on the radio?

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.830
Hey, Miss Minare. Are you there?

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.410
Hello, Nakahara? It's me, it's me.
Do you have a minute?

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:36.660
Hey, remember what you said earlier?
Could I take you up on that?

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.080
Yeah, that's it!

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.410
--Ritsukoooo!
--Huh? Wait, hold on, I'll text you.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:44.500
Come to that guy's place
where we dropped off the salmon

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.330
and wait until I signal you to come in.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:50.200
Do you own a stun gun? Bring it if you do.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.370
Forgive me! Ritsuko!

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.700
I've seen that pose in <i>The First Step</i>.

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.660
Mr. Oki, please stay with us.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.540
Could you tell us what happened
with the woman named Ritsuko?

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.950
We're good to go.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.450
Okay.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:11.330
All right.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:12.580
Huh?

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.700
"Episode 7: I Want to Cry"
Ritsuko is...

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:51.830
Ritsuko is...

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:56.910
Ritsuko Azohara is a woman I met
when I lived in Tokyo.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:00.660
She's a third generation Slavic woman
who loves manga and hot springs.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.870
We met on a Dogashima hot springs bus tour.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:07.700
As the young ones among the group,
we naturally started to chat.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:12.120
Eventually, we went off on our own
to check out the hot springs.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:15.450
Oh, what a wonderful start to a romance!

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:19.620
Well, I don't know about romance...

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.080
Because, you know...

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.660
We never crossed that line...

00:03:25.660 --> 00:03:29.160
Actually, everything started from that fact.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.080
So you're saying you wanted to cross that line.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:42.910
I confessed my feelings for her
a year after we met.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.620
I'm flattered...

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:50.870
Let's go to a secluded, open-air,
co-ed hot springs... Just the two of us.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.200
And there...

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.870
How romantic!

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:57.250
That sounds fishy, and plus you'd be
a nuisance to other customers.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.540
So, then...

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:02.080
We chose the hot springs by throwing a dart
on the map while holding each other's hands.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.830
Just hearing about it makes me wanna vomit...

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:07.250
"Yamagata Prefecture"
It's Zao.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:10.000
The open-air co-ed hot springs in Zao is...

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.040
"Kamoshika Hot Springs"
"Mount Zao Okama (Five Color Pond)"
Kamoshika hot springs.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:14.080
"Kamoshika Hot Springs"
"Mount Zao Okama (Five Color Pond)"
Kamoshika hot springs is such a cute name.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.700
"Kamoshika Hot Springs"
"Mount Zao Okama (Five Color Pond)"
I don't know if it's cute...

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:18.950
But what I do know is that it's
a very secluded hot springs.

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:22.080
From the Zao Echo Line's
Sainokawara parking lot,

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.750
we walked off the beaten path
for an hour and a half.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.080
We were headed for an open-air hot
springs located halfway up the cliff

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.620
where we were at risk of falling rocks.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:31.660
It's a great nature setting
that rejects all humanity!

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:34.370
It's the perfect spot for
lovemaking under the stars.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.040
You would think so.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:41.870
But despite its location, people still
make it out there during tourist season.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:43.750
So that's why...

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:47.830
Ah... In order to secure...

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.450
...a completely secluded hot springs...

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:54.160
We chose to go in the winter
when there're no tourists.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:58.370
We also chose a windless day so the
volcanic gases would accumulate better.

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:01.200
We did all that to avoid encountering anyone.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:06.700
I see. So you carefully concocted
a situation that screams out disaster.

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:17.830
That was the first time I laid eyes on...

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.290
...Ritsuko's beautiful body...

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:29.160
Our fingers intertwined...

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:32.160
And our lips drew closer...

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.580
And then...

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:39.450
My memory draws a blank beyond that moment.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.870
You can absolutely blame the gas for that.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:45.830
When I came to,

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:51.700
I was rescued and resting at a
house nearby Gaga hot springs.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:53.790
What happened to the woman who was with me...?

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.700
Huh? We only found you.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:59.700
Boy, what a sight. We found you
on the ground butt naked.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:07.120
Even when spring came around,
they couldn't find Ritsuko's body.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:11.870
She must be wandering around Zao
somewhere right now, as we speak.

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:16.290
I haven't been able to retrieve
my heart from the mountains, either,

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.910
ever since that winter...

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:19.160
Excuse me.

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:21.080
I've got a question for you.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.000
Yes.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:28.120
According to the fax you sent to Moiwayama
Radio, it clearly says that she died.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:31.870
Does this mean you're sure
that she is, deep down?

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:33.910
That Miss Ritsuko's dead?

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:39.620
I was completely distraught
when I wrote that, to be honest.

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:42.410
But, well, I don't know...

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:44.790
When I try to think, my head just...

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:48.200
This room has the same layout as mine, right?

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:50.750
Mr. Oki, do you have a flashlight?

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:53.580
Oh... Um... Where did I put it?

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.120
Oh, Miss Minare. I brought one.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:59.580
I brought it just in case--since it was
a nighttime investigation.

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:00.700
What are you doing?

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:06.290
Mr. Oki, I have no idea why you came to me
for help after listening to my program...

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:07.910
I'm borrowing this, by the way.

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:13.370
But since I've never been to the spirit world,
I tend to come up with realistic solutions

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:16.500
before I think about how
to return from that world.

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:17.410
Ah!

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:20.330
Here it is. Miss Minare, please be careful.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:23.500
You bet! Don't worry.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.410
Just checking if it works.

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:32.750
This reminds me of a scene from <i>The Grudge</i>.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:36.660
There's typically a feint at first...

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:39.450
They don't just come out like that...

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:40.500
Whoa! It's there!

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:43.620
What did you see? A ghost? A zombie?!

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:46.250
A specter? An evil spirit?!

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:49.160
What? Um... A fly...

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.410
Oh...

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:52.790
A fly?

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:54.790
A fly.

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:57.830
Let's see... It goes that way over there...

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:59.500
So I go this way...

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:02.200
Agh... Oh, huh?!

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:05.200
I need to focus or else I'll lose
consciousness from this stench!

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:09.410
And... What's with this
ridiculous swarm of flies?

00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:11.750
Is this a bug disaster movie from the 70's?

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:18.160
And let's be real. This isn't a situation where
a young maiden can keep her sanity, right?

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.830
Ah! Let's move!

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:22.250
Ahhh! I'm not giving up!

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:24.870
It's easy to tell where she is.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.870
Ah! Whoa!

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:28.250
It reeks!

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:32.000
Shoot! My 3,980-yen Onmyoji costume
from the discount store!

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:33.910
They don't sell such a thing!

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:36.580
Huh? This sound...

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:41.040
I heard it right before
the spoiled juices dripped down.

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:42.660
So basically...

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:47.200
Things are not as scary as they seem.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:51.410
This is the sound of the upper tenant
using the shower or hot water supply.

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:55.580
So this leak is the reason
for water getting everywhere.

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:57.000
Huh?

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:01.200
From what I can see, this water's clear.

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:07.500
What makes this water spoil...?

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:08.580
Huh?

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:14.040
Dammit...

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:19.290
One... Two, three, four, five, six...

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:23.790
That's enough to bag up a petit woman's body...

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:29.000
Huh?

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.700
"Go inside and hold down the guy.

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:35.830
I think the door is unlocked.
He might take Mizuho hostage.

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:38.750
If that happens, say, 'Dammit, you coward.'

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:40.750
That'll be my signal to break
through the ceiling"...

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:41.830
Ah...

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:46.370
Dammit! Is this a divine calling
for me to switch to journalism?

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:46.910
--Yes, this is the Sapporo Kita Police.

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:48.580
--Hey! Who the hell are you?
--Yes, this is the Sapporo Kita Police.

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:51.000
--All right, just calm down.
--Um, I'd like to report that
a rotting body was found...

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.160
--S-Stop!
--Um, I'd like to report that
a rotting body was found...

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.870
What should I do?

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:00.370
This is the main office. Please respond.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:05.450
I didn't kill anyone... It wasn't me...
I didn't kill anyone...

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:06.700
It wasn't me.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:09.450
I climbed into the attic
from the room's ceiling.

00:10:09.450 --> 00:10:10.660
In that outfit?

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:12.790
Yes, in this outfit.

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:15.080
It wasn't me.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:17.580
I didn't kill anyone...

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:19.750
Evil was destroyed...

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:26.540
Wait, evil...? Was he an evil man...?

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:30.040
Do I even have the right to judge him like that?

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:39.500
If justice can settle a tragedy
caused by trouble between lovers,

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:42.620
what a wretched world this is.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:46.160
His crime...

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:51.750
...will be detailed by the police soon.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.160
Morning.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:54.450
Good morning.

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:55.750
Morning.

00:10:56.500 --> 00:11:00.580
Autumn is already here. How is everyone doing?

00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:05.700
Last night, since I had an urge, I watched
the uncut version of In the <i>Realm of the Senses</i>.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:11.330
Sada Abe said, "I have no doubt other
women have thought of doing what I did.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:17.370
They just don't do it." I think I've come
to understand her words now.

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:22.830
Sada Abe cut off her lover's
genitals while making love.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:24.950
Can you call that love?

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.290
I heard you had quite a night last night.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.410
I'll say...

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:33.950
There was a dark abyss, a ridiculous
swarm of flies, spoiled black water,

00:11:33.950 --> 00:11:37.830
an indescribable stench... It was too much.

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.330
Lovecraft?

00:11:41.290 --> 00:11:44.870
During the police investigation,
one of the officers stopped by.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:50.250
They told me it's most likely a mutilated body,
but it's too far decomposed now...

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:51.200
Oh, no.

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:53.870
But, according to what you said, Miss Minare,

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:59.000
they were a tad strange
but a happy couple nonetheless, right?

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:01.660
Why would he kill his lover?

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:06.580
Oh, come on, Acting Manager. You lack
the imagination and the pheromones.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:07.700
Pheromones...

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:10.750
The crucial fact was how the
woman was of Slavic descent.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:14.830
What does that have to do with anything?
Plus, you never told me that until now.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.370
So, it turns out...

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:21.080
...she was a spy sent by the Russian
foreign intelligence agency.

00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:25.410
Of course, getting close to Mr. Oki
was part of her plan.

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:29.700
There's always a reason behind a
woman who's with a desperate man.

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:31.250
That's harsh.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:36.370
But actually, Mr. Oki already had his suspicion.

00:12:36.370 --> 00:12:39.830
That's why he was so bold
to take her to a secluded area

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:42.950
to question her without anyone listening.

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:47.660
Ritsuko.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.870
I need to ask you... Um...

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.370
Who are you?

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:54.370
What do you mean?

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:55.790
I'm...

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:58.540
I've checked the public housing
you said you grew up in,

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:00.910
and the junior high school
you said you attended...

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:05.910
I've looked everywhere, but a girl
named Ritsuko Azohara never existed...

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.410
Explain this to me.

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:10.370
I'm ready to accept whatever you tell me.

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:13.750
With all this gas, by night--

00:13:13.750 --> 00:13:17.120
Before he could finish,
she was already pointing a gun at him.

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:21.410
She was trained to kill
if she was ever suspected.

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:25.500
But after all, either her emotional attachment
prevented her from pulling the trigger...

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:29.250
...or the gas made her too woozy to function...

00:13:29.250 --> 00:13:31.120
That remains a mystery...

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:41.410
But before she could pull the trigger,
Mr. Oki bashed her head with a rock.

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:47.580
If he can manage to do that, that guy's
got serial killer-like characteristics, too.

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:53.410
Well, I'm impressed with the police.
They figured all of that out over night?

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:54.540
Of course not!

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:59.950
I was just saying it'd be romantic if that
were the case. It's like a Greek tragedy.

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:01.160
How exactly?

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:02.080
Oh.

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:07.450
Hello?

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:10.700
Oh, yes. Thank you for last night.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:11.830
Yes...

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:17.160
Right now?! That's a bit...

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:22.700
Yes, 3:30 PM would be better...

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:26.200
Oh, is that okay? Great, I'll be there then.

00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:27.200
Was that Mr. Mato?

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:29.580
No, that was the Sapporo Kita Police.

00:14:29.580 --> 00:14:31.910
They wanted to confirm something with me.

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:34.040
I'm going over there after the lunch shift.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:36.040
I wonder what they're going to ask.

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:38.290
They'll probably ask about my
physical relationship with Mr. Oki.

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:38.870
What?!

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:43.870
Well, you know. Depending on that,
I could become a suspect, too.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:46.580
You sound kind of excited.

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:50.120
Excuse me. I've got a question for you.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:51.040
Yes.

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:56.290
--According to the fax you sent to Moiwayama
Radio, it clearly says that she died.

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.120
--The sound's really muffled.
--According to the fax you sent to Moiwayama
Radio, it clearly says that she died.

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:58.790
--The sound's really muffled.
--Does this mean you're sure that she is,
deep down? That Miss Ritsuko's dead?

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:01.500
--It won't be usable unless
it's heavily processed.
--Does this mean you're sure that she is,
deep down? That Miss Ritsuko's dead?

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:06.160
I'm sorry. I should've told her to
take the recorder out of her pocket.

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:10.000
Whoa!

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:12.870
Should we use the sound from the camcorder?

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:17.830
I'm sure we can pull it off without it. You both
must have a lot to say about what happened.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:20.540
You have no idea how crazy it was!

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:23.750
The smell wouldn't come off,
so I ended up taking three showers!

00:15:24.750 --> 00:15:27.410
It's hard to say this when there's a victim...

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:30.830
But this could potentially be used as
advertising material for the program.

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:32.290
Oh?

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:38.950
Right now, Wave, Listen to Me! is being
advertised on the station's homepage.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:43.950
But even avid radio listeners
rarely access the station's website.

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:48.330
It's a whole other story
if it's advertised on the waves.

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:51.330
--News Pickup! It's time for
the nine o'clock news.
--Regarding the body-dumping
incident mentioned earlier,

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:54.700
--An incident occurred at an apartment
in Sapporo around 11 PM last night.
--the body was actually discovered
by an MRS personality.

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:56.370
Oh, I see.

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:59.370
The news will air six times
until the next broadcast.

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:02.750
And if we can get some follow-up news
as well, we can expect quite the--

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:05.830
Huh? Hey, look who's here.

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:08.750
Ugh...

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.080
Huh?

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:14.080
Ah, I forgot all about it.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:17.160
Odori Park's Zombie Walk
started today, didn't it?

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:20.200
Pretty sure that doesn't start for a while...

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:32.910
In the end, what Miss Minare
and I experienced that night

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:36.830
never made it on the news
as a body-abandoning murder case,

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:40.120
or on the front page of the national press.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:41.080
"Local News: Could it be a body-abandoning
murder case?! An unexpected truth..."

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:44.080
"Local News: Could it be a body-abandoning
murder case?! An unexpected truth..."
It only made it on a little
blurb on a local news website

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:50.120
"1: Chinghis Khan: What...?"
"2: Anonymous: Typical woman."
and was mentioned in a thread
on an online forum.

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:54.200
And then...

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:58.620
On the day of recording the second
broadcast of Wave, Listen to Me!...

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:15.200
Minare Koda's Wave, Listen to Me!

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:20.330
It's the dead of night at 3:30 AM.

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:26.450
I question everyone who's tuned in right now.
What are you expecting to hear?

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:32.450
How do you do? I'm Minare Koda,
a new personality at MRS.

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:38.120
So, actually... This isn't my first time
on air, technically... Um, well...

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:38.870
--So, before we get into talking about

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.120
--She's inarticulate today.
--So, before we get into talking about

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:46.540
the program's concept and what
I'll be doing for future segments...

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:49.830
I must first apologize to a certain gentleman

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:52.870
and the people who got involved
in an incident I caused.

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:57.040
So... As was mentioned on the
web version of Hokkaido News,

00:17:57.040 --> 00:18:01.580
some of you might know about this already...

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:05.080
About the lumps of meat
found in the attic last night...

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:09.620
Turns out, it wasn't a human body.

00:18:09.620 --> 00:18:10.870
What?

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:12.040
What?!

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:15.370
Since it was cut into pieces and decomposed,

00:18:15.370 --> 00:18:19.330
we didn't realize it until we
sent it to the coroner's...

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:24.330
Long story short, it was processed mutton meat.

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:26.200
So there is no case.

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:27.870
O-Oh...

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.250
And, another thing.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:36.120
Following your report, we went through
Mr. Shinji Oki's room to recover the meat

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:39.160
and recklessly arrested him.

00:18:39.160 --> 00:18:40.000
"Minare Koda"       "Female College Student"
"Vacant Room"             "Shinji Oki"
and recklessly arrested him.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:44.160
"Minare Koda"       "Female College Student"
"Vacant Room"             "Shinji Oki"
But when the manager of the
building showed us the layout later,

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:49.410
"Minare Koda"       "Female College Student"
"Vacant Room"             "Shinji Oki"
we figured out that the meat
was located right under your room.

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:54.200
So I suspect this is what actually happened...

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:58.450
When I moved from my hometown
of Kushiro to Sapporo,

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:04.250
my parents sent me with 50 kg
of bone-in mutton and jars of fruit wine.

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:07.200
Since all of that was impossible
to store in the fridge,

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:11.870
I put them in the storage space under
the floor as a temporary measure

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:14.080
and completely forgot about their existence.

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:18.120
Eventually, the storage space
gave in to the weight

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:21.120
and the food started to rot
in between the floors.

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:23.500
And whenever the neighbor across took a bath,

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:27.120
the water would leak and carry
the rotten juices which turned it black.

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:31.200
And that's how it oozed out in
various spots of the lower floor.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:37.160
Whether this was my fault or the management
who failed to maintain the building...

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:39.450
I'd say I'm on the innocent
side of the spectrum.

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:41.080
Innocent...?

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:43.000
You're completely guilty.

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:44.700
Agreed.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:48.330
So... that's what happened...

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:50.330
And although we're equally at fault...

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:55.040
I jumped the gun and deemed an innocent
man a murderer and called the police.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:20:00.290
Because of that, four police cars showed up
and caused a troubling scene for my neighbors.

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:05.120
And for that, I'd like to take this moment
to apologize. I'm truly sorry.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:14.290
So, uh, anyway... I know I mentioned
murder and aliens last time...

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:19.080
But at this very moment, reality seems

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:21.290
even more bizarre to me.

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:25.370
Well, on that note, let's turn things around.

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:29.540
It's time for our regular missing person
segment, Listen, On the Wave!

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:31.540
Regular segment?

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:33.700
Was that in the script?

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:37.830
No, it's not. It only says "Talk about
that night" on the cue sheet, too.

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:41.000
--Our first missing person is Ritsuko Azohara.
--And anyway, why do a missing persons
segment during a dead-of-night program

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:44.120
--She's a 22-year-old third generation
Slavic woman.
--with only a few listeners?

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:46.330
She's about 157 cm tall and went missing

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:49.870
in the middle of January
last year in Shibata-gun, Miyagi.

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:52.200
It's nearby Zao hot springs village.

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:58.120
"What do you think?"
If you know anyone who fits this description,
please contact this radio program.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:21:02.000
You can contact us by e-mail, fax,
postcard, or mail. Whatever suits you.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:03.370
"Fine, I'll drop the charges."

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:09.830
"Relief..."
So... Today's the first official broadcast
of Minare Koda's Wave, Listen to Me!

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:13.450
So... Today's the first official broadcast
of Minare Koda's Wave, Listen to Me!

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:18.160
This program is for people who've
caused countless troubles for others.

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:24.200
Those who hurt someone precious to them,
those who consistently choose the wrong path...

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:28.290
But don't want their life to go to waste!

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:34.040
"I just want to redeem myself"! For all you
hopeless cases who think like that,

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:35.910
I want this program to be for you!

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:41.410
--She did mention she wanted to make
this program "fluffy as a towel," right?
--Since I can't stop crying,
I think I'm gonna go now.

00:21:41.410 --> 00:21:43.330
--She did mention she wanted to make
this program "fluffy as a towel," right?
--I'm sure everyone's made mistakes like I have.
Although, I think my case was a bit extreme.

00:21:43.330 --> 00:21:49.620
--Yes, but it seems like Miss Minare's slowly
being strangled by a silk thread.
--I'm sure everyone's made mistakes like I have.
Although, I think my case was a bit extreme.

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:52.450
--Well, she's the one doing
the strangling, too.
--But the point is, everyone, please don't
give up on recovering from that trauma!

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:54.290
See you next time!

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:56.160
We're sponsored by...

00:21:56.950 --> 00:21:58.910
Whoops, there aren't any sponsors.

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:30.750
"Next Episode"

00:23:30.750 --> 00:23:32.250
"Preview"
Hello, Dad?

00:23:32.250 --> 00:23:35.200
"Preview"
Minare, why are you calling this late at night?

00:23:35.200 --> 00:23:37.500
Well, I don't know why
I didn't ask you this earlier...

00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:40.000
But what does my name, "Minare," mean?

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:42.700
The day has come to finally tell you.

00:23:42.700 --> 00:23:45.200
What, is there some deep meaning behind it?

00:23:45.200 --> 00:23:46.750
Say the syllables backwards.

00:23:46.750 --> 00:23:47.450
Renami.

00:23:47.450 --> 00:23:48.500
Take out the "na."

00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:49.200
Remi.

00:23:49.200 --> 00:23:50.250
There, that's the truth.

00:23:50.250 --> 00:23:51.870
That makes no sense!

00:23:51.870 --> 00:23:54.000
Next, on <i>Wave, Listen to Me!</i>

00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:59.000
"I Can't Tell You Over the Phone."

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:01.950
"See you next time!"
